      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#2 · Q27:2937–2950 governing the assignments (human-amplified: yes); C39",
          "title": "Colour acquires a passage; the joins stay visible",
          "italic": "The seams embody method: choosing and joining materials already determines how the source can become visible — a source enters because its operation changes what the whole can disclose.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Each pane has a material, density, colour and angle: placement permits some transmission, bends or colours what passes, leaves something obstructed. Removing every difference in pursuit of neutrality would also remove the transformations through which the composition becomes articulate. The original quilt distinguishes the window from an opaque mosaic: the mosaic arranges fragments into a surface image; the window works through transmission and obstruction as well as arrangement. The lead cames carry the joins — holding neighbouring panes in relation while marking where one",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "passage ends and another begins; in the epistemic construction the seams retain source provenance, historical discontinuity, translation limits, contradiction and changes of register. These figure MEF, whose office C39 defines: a lens changes a question, a permissible inference or an act of judgment while keeping its conditions inspectable. The correction matters at the material seam itself: the lead is assigned to the refractive apparatus and QL to the light's harmonic order — MEF makes distinctions available within that order without standing outside it as a certifying superior.\n\nOccurrences: the pane placements (#2); the lead's held joins (#2, reused at #4's comparison); the corrected apparatus/light assignment (#2, carried through #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
