      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#3–#4 · P5's invested reading; Gebser pp.1–3, 11–21, 255–58; A04; A16/A22; Symbolon Dynamics",
          "title": "The image appears; changing light discloses the construction",
          "italic": "Recognition proceeds through exact differences among the projections towards the order they disclose — neither averaging differences nor adding them into a final picture.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The coloured display is produced through the relation of light and made aperture, appearing in an interior and encountered from a position. Looking only at the glass recovers matter and arrangement while missing the event of transmission; looking only at the cast image conceals the glass, its joins and placement. The situated image is pratibimba, and its danger begins when availability becomes a claim to possess the source. The viewer is implicated: body, position, attention and concern enter what is seen — P5's demand for an invested reading of text and subtext. As sun, pane, angle, room and viewer change, the projected colour",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "changes: a later display makes visible a region previously obscured and can expose an aberration the first view concealed. The order recognisable across the transformations belongs to Bimba/QL; the appearances remain pratibimbas. The 180°→360° movement names the contextual turn — the first-, second- and third-person positions ceasing to claim isolated completeness as their joint conditions become available. The atlas carries the complementary discipline: a chart-transition is not light passing through glass; each whole retains the operation the other cannot perform; an attractor organising trajectories is not an atlas of charts.\n\nOccurrences: the changing sun and revealed region (#4); the implicated viewer (#3, #4); the atlas/window distinction (#4, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
